            <ArticleTitle>[Papillomatosis of the mitral valve as an unusual cause of myocardial ischemia. Description of a case and review of the literature].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Papilloma is a rare primary heart tumour; only 75 cases have been reported and most were casual findings at autopsy. We describe another case of this tumour in a 9 years girl. The neoformation had produced a picture of angina pectoris, followed by death due to an occluded left coronary orifice. To our knowledge, this is the first report of this type of tumour with electrocardiographic documentation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
